---
title: Chili
servings: 9
image: https://www.sipandfeast.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/classic-chili-recipe-5.jpg
---

Cook @onion{1}(diced), @ground beef{2%lbs}, and @bell peppers{3}(sliced) on the stove in a #large pot{}.

Add @diced tomatoes{2%cans}(plain works, but getting fire roasted etc. is fun) and @beans{3%cans}(draining half of the liquid of the cans. Ideally, 1 dark red, 1 light red, 1 chili. You can use black peans or pinto, but avoid white peans or garbanzo beans).

Add plenty of sauces and seasonings to your tastes: @?jalapeño peppers{2-3} or other spicy peppers of your choice, @?salt{}, @?pepper{}, @?Italian Seasoning{}, @?onion powder{}, @?garlic powder{}, @?chili powder{}, @?cayenne pepper{}, @?paprika{}, @?worcester sauce{}, etc.

Simmer and keep hot for approximately ~{1%hour}.

Taste test to see if you need any additional sauces or seasonings. If all is good, serve with @?sour cream{} and @?shredded cheese{}.